    <!-- SECTION: SCHOLASTIC JOURNEY & SYSTEM PROFILE DOSSIER -->
    <section class="section about-section" aria-label="Personal Background and Philosophy">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="about-grid">
          <!-- Left Column: Detailed Scholastic Narrative -->
          <div class="about-editorial reveal-item">
            <div class="section-meta">
              <span class="section-index">// 01.1</span>
              <span class="section-tag">SCHOLASTIC RIGOR &amp; PHILOSOPHY</span>
            </div>

            <div class="editorial-body">
              <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-luxury); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.6rem); color: var(--text-primary); margin: 24px 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; font-weight: 600;">
                The Foundation: Respecting the Machine
              </h2>
              <p>
                When many aspiring developers enter software creation, the instinct is often to immediately reach for heavy high-level frameworks and automated boilerplates. My academic path has reinforced a more deliberate philosophy: <strong>learn the mechanics first</strong>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Studying <strong>C programming</strong> in my BCA curriculum taught me what actually happens when software runs—how memory addresses are allocated and freed, why pointer arithmetic matters, how data structures like linked lists, stacks, and binary trees organize information, and how algorithmic efficiency dictates real-world responsiveness.
              </p>

              <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-luxury); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.6rem); color: var(--text-primary); margin: 36px 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; font-weight: 600;">
                The Medium: The Open Web
              </h2>
              <p>
                The browser is humanity's most accessible creative canvas. By taking the mathematical discipline learned in computer science and applying it to modern web standards—semantic HTML5, fluid clamp equations in CSS, vanilla JavaScript, and WebGL—I strive to build websites that feel alive, responsive, and unmistakably premium.
              </p>
              <p>
                Every project I undertake is built with care: zero unnecessary framework bloat, respectful typography, and interfaces designed to provide a genuine aesthetic experience.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Right Column: System Profile Dossier -->
          <div class="about-dossier-col reveal-item">
            <div class="dossier-panel" data-tilt>
              <div class="dossier-header">
                <span>PROFILE DOSSIER // ZEERAK SIDDIQUI</span>
              </div>
              <div class="specs-table">
                <div class="specs-row">
                  <span class="specs-label">DEGREE</span>
                  <span class="specs-val">Bachelor of Computer Applications (BCA)</span>
                </div>
                <div class="specs-row">
